    why: "One failed-logins number has to become two facts — whole hours and leftover minutes — and a threshold check has to mean exactly what an analyst thinks it means. // and % are the split-and-rebuild pair, and precedence decides what an expression REALLY computed; a log triage tool that misreads either silently misjudges severity.",
    output: "7 // 2 is 3 whole shares with 7 % 2 = 1 left over, and 3 * 2 + 1 rebuilds 7 — the check line proves the split. 2 + 3 * 2 ** 2 computes 14 because ** binds first (4), then * (12), then +; the parenthesised version computes 20. The chained 1 <= 443 <= 1024 prints True, confirming a standard port range test in one expression.",
